CVE-2021-20190 (CWE-502): jackson-databind allowed the javax.swing.JTextPane /
javax.swing.JEditorPane gadget classes to be resolved as polymorphic subtypes
when default typing is enabled, enabling SSRF / DoS via crafted type ids.

The jackson-databind 2.3.x branch predates upstream SubTypeValidator, so the
Root.io 2.3.1 backport enforces the gadget denylist inline in
ClassNameIdResolver._typeFromId (see the DEFAULT_NO_DESER_CLASS_NAMES set and
_checkIllegalType). The javax.swing.JTextPane / JEditorPane entries required by
CVE-2021-20190 are already carried in that denylist (added alongside the
CVE-2020-36181 backport) and are rejected at the type-id resolution chokepoint
that covers both Id.CLASS (ClassNameIdResolver) and Id.MINIMAL_CLASS
(MinimalClassNameIdResolver, which delegates via super._typeFromId) as well as
the generic-canonical branch. This patch therefore contributes the regression
test that pins the CVE-2021-20190 behavior for this version; the deserialization
fix itself is already present in the accumulated 2.3.1 hook.

